// 006.8 (D37, #45, #17): `Debt` gives each raising its own obligation ID, independent deadline,
// and remaining balance reduced by partial payments until discharged at zero.
Fact tenant Identified by Tess
Fact landlord Identified by Lou
Act bill-rent Actor landlord Recipient tenant Holds when True
Act pay-rent Actor tenant Recipient landlord Related to int, payment : USD Holds when True

Debt rent-debt Holder tenant Claimant landlord Amount $1,200.00
  Raised by bill-rent
  Paid by pay-rent
  Due within 5
.
bill-rent(Lou, Tess).
?rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 1).
?(rent-debt-remaining(1) == $1,200.00).
@ 3.
// Second month billed at t=3 gets its own ID (2) and its own 5-day clock:
bill-rent(Lou, Tess).
?rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 2).
@ 5.
// At t=5, month 1 is violated (5 - 0 >= 5), while month 2 is NOT violated yet (5 - 3 < 5)!
?violated rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 1).
?!violated rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 2).
// Partial payment of $500 on month 1 leaves $700 still due; remaining $700 discharges month 1:
pay-rent(Tess, Lou, 1, $500.00).
?(rent-debt-remaining(1) == $700.00).
?rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 1).
pay-rent(Tess, Lou, 1, $700.00).
?(rent-debt-remaining(1) == $0.00).
?!rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 1).
?rent-debt(Tess, Lou, 2).
